s, including N-deacetylation and N-sulfation. The encoded protein may be localized to the Golgi. [provided by RefSeq, Feb 2009].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"P52849","text":"Essential bifunctional enzyme that catalyzes both the N-deacetylation and the N-sulfation of glucosamine (GlcNAc) of the glycosaminoglycan in heparan sulfate (By similarity). Exhibits N-deacetylase activity (PubMed:16343444). Modifies the GlcNAc-GlcA disaccharide repeating sugar backbone to make N-sulfated heparosan, a prerequisite substrate for later modifications in heparin biosynthesis (By similarity). Plays a role in determining the extent and pattern of sulfation of heparan sulfate (By similarity). Required for the exosomal release of SDCBP, CD63 and syndecan (PubMed:22660413). Essential for the biosynthesis of sulfated heparin in mast cells, thereby enabling proper secretory granule formation and storage of mast-cell proteases (By similarity)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}